1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,700
Completing your referrers' own report forms
from TM3 notes – for Blue Heart Clinics.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:11,059
You told us your MLCs and insurers send their own report forms,
with different layouts, questions, headings and formats.

3
00:00:11,099 --> 00:00:17,099
You need that specific form completed from the patient's
registration details and physiotherapy notes – not a generic report.

4
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:19,700
This walkthrough answers your five questions in turn.

5
00:00:20,009 --> 00:00:23,962
Your question 1 of 5 – You asked: “Whether the system
can work from different MLC/insurer report templates.”

6
00:00:24,351 --> 00:00:32,291
Three of your referrers' own forms, each in its own layout:
two Word forms and a fillable PDF (fictional examples).

7
00:00:32,341 --> 00:00:39,756
A new referrer sends a form you haven't seen before.
Your staff upload it once, exactly as received.

8
00:00:39,806 --> 00:00:46,666
The system reads the blank form and identifies each question and answer
space – no patient data is involved. (sped up – real time about 23 s)

9
00:00:46,716 --> 00:00:54,064
17 questions found in Meridian's form
– 1 flagged for a person to check.

10
00:00:54,114 --> 00:01:03,592
For each question it proposes the source – TM3 registration,
the notes, the clinician's opinion or sign-off.

11
00:01:03,642 --> 00:01:12,332
Your team confirms it once; it is then reused
for every patient that referrer sends.

12
00:01:12,382 --> 00:01:18,890
Yes – each referrer's form is set up once, confirmed
by your team, then reused for every patient.

13
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:24,393
Your question 3 of 5 – You asked: “Whether it can use TM3 registration
details and physiotherapy notes without us duplicating data manually.”

14
00:01:24,784 --> 00:01:30,591
Your clinic system – here our Simulated TM3 sandbox:
fictional demo data, not affiliated with TM3.

15
00:01:30,641 --> 00:01:37,300
Megan's record: registration details, 11 appointments
and 10 clinical notes. One click opens the form tool.

16
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:41,421
Imported automatically – 10 notes,
11 appointments, 6 outcome scores.

17
00:01:41,461 --> 00:01:44,560
Nothing is retyped, and every call to TM3 is logged.

18
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:52,213
Yes – imported from TM3, nothing retyped. Today via a TM3
export; a direct link is subject to TM3 providing access.

19
00:01:52,866 --> 00:01:57,720
Your question 2 of 5 – You asked: “Whether it can complete
the report in the original format/layout sent to us.”

20
00:01:58,107 --> 00:02:05,320
Choose the referrer's form – Harrow & Pike's medico-legal form
is suggested, because Megan's referral came from Harrow & Pike.

21
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:11,891
Registration details are filled in by code; each clinical answer is drafted
from Megan's notes, citing its note. (sped up – real time about 12 s)

22
00:02:11,941 --> 00:02:17,060
16 questions: 8 filled from TM3
records, 4 drafted from the notes,

23
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:23,353
4 left for the clinician – red “Blocked”
marks a check to clear before approval.

24
00:02:23,403 --> 00:02:28,191
Harrow & Pike's own Word form, filled
in – their layout, headings and boxes.

25
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,962
Marked DRAFT until a clinician approves it.

26
00:02:31,012 --> 00:02:37,836
Yes – answers are written into the referrer's
own document; the layout is unchanged.

27
00:02:39,124 --> 00:02:44,277
Your question 4 of 5 – You asked: “How clinician review, amendment
and approval would work before the final report is issued.”

28
00:02:44,666 --> 00:02:50,477
Every drafted answer cites its source. Click a
citation to check it against the original note.

29
00:02:50,527 --> 00:02:56,695
Suppose someone adds a statement the notes
don't support – here, a recovery date…

30
00:02:56,745 --> 00:03:05,004
…the checks flag it at once and block approval: the date isn't in
the cited note, and the clinician never recorded that opinion.

31
00:03:05,054 --> 00:03:09,140
Undo the edit and the flags clear.

32
00:03:09,190 --> 00:03:13,567
Megan's notes record no prognosis,
so it is left blank – not guessed

33
00:03:13,607 --> 00:03:19,063
– and blocks approval until the treating
physiotherapist writes it in her own words.

34
00:03:19,113 --> 00:03:26,406
She answers the other opinion questions and resolves the
remaining checks – every edit is logged with who and when.

35
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:37,040
16 of 16 answered and clear. Approval records her name, HCPC
number (fictional), typed signature and four attestations.

36
00:03:39,438 --> 00:03:46,626
Approved: final and read-only – download it as
Word or PDF, or save it to the patient's record.

37
00:03:46,676 --> 00:03:50,994
The final PDF as downloaded: their layout, TM3 details by code,

38
00:03:51,034 --> 00:03:55,945
answers from the notes, her own
prognosis and approval – no DRAFT mark.

39
00:03:55,995 --> 00:04:02,505
Nothing is issued until the treating clinician has
reviewed, amended and approved it – every change is logged.

40
00:04:02,555 --> 00:04:06,811
Your question 1 of 5 – your example – You wrote: “…another may ask
similar clinical questions in a completely different structure.”

41
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:13,370
Same patient, same notes – now Northfield Assurance's fillable
PDF, with similar questions in a different structure.

42
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:18,180
The system drafts Megan's answers again – this time to
Northfield's own questions. (sped up – real time about 9 s)

43
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:24,739
12 of 17 answered and clear after drafting. As before,
she adds her opinions and Northfield's claim number…

44
00:04:24,789 --> 00:04:35,809
…and answers what doesn't apply (“Not applicable”, 0 further
sessions): all 17 answered and clear before she approves.

45
00:04:35,859 --> 00:04:42,217
Your example: one referrer asks for prognosis, functional
restrictions and treatment recommendations in one format;

46
00:04:42,257 --> 00:04:48,433
another asks similar questions in a different structure.
Same notes – each form completed in its own structure.

47
00:04:48,483 --> 00:04:54,649
Yes – same notes, each referrer's form completed in
its own structure, whether Word or fillable PDF.

48
00:04:54,699 --> 00:04:58,254
Your question 3 of 5 – back into the patient's record
– You asked: “…without us duplicating data manually.”

49
00:04:58,663 --> 00:05:06,921
One click – “Save to clinic record” – files it back: in the
simulated TM3, Megan's Documents tab now lists both completed forms.

50
00:05:06,971 --> 00:05:14,525
Filed back to the record. With your real TM3 this needs
TM3 access – until then, it's one download and attach.

51
00:05:14,575 --> 00:05:18,229
Your question 5 of 5 – You asked: “Whether patient
data would remain secure and GDPR compliant.”

52
00:05:20,141 --> 00:05:26,569
You can see exactly what the drafting service
receives: the name becomes [CLAIMANT];

53
00:05:26,609 --> 00:05:30,075
no date of birth, address or contact details.

54
00:05:30,125 --> 00:05:38,783
The Security & GDPR page sets out the rest – what this demo
does today, and what is in place before real patient data.

55
00:05:39,567 --> 00:05:43,486
Your question 5: what will be in place
before any real patient data is used.

56
00:05:43,526 --> 00:05:47,602
A Data Processing Agreement and DPIA, UK
hosting, encryption, two-factor login.

57
00:05:47,642 --> 00:05:51,967
Minimised data under contract, an audit
trail, clinician approval, agreed deletion.

58
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:56,834
Your five questions, answered. Templates:
yes, set up once. Original layout: yes.

59
00:05:56,874 --> 00:06:01,354
TM3 data: yes, no retyping – today via TM3
export; direct link subject to TM3 access.

60
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:05,967
Nothing issued before clinician approval.
Security: in place before real patient data.

61
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:11,156
Your next step: send us an anonymised MLC report
form and the matching anonymised clinical notes.

62
00:06:11,196 --> 00:06:14,967
We'll run them through this process and
send you the completed draft to review.
